  "limits": [
    "Each case stages 134 high-HP enemies, 350 hostile and 50 friendly slow persistent projectiles, a 42-item replayed inventory and 17 upgrade deltas. Actual initial material piles are capped/merged by production drop logic. The setup is synthetic and is not a saved R21 world state.",
    "The CPU profiler is non-Deep with allocation callstacks disabled in the recorded cases. Profiler GC.Alloc samples have overhead; lowering allocation also lowers profiling overhead. Diagnostic frame durations cannot be presented as production FPS gains.",
    "Captures request two seconds after three seconds of warmup. They contain only 3, 4 and 16 telemetry frames; their percentiles are descriptive samples, not stable performance benchmarks.",
    "The exported profiler contains one more boundary frame than native telemetry in each case. Simulation-tick denominators come from agreeing subsystem marker call counts, not exported frame totals.",
    "GC.GetAllocatedBytesForCurrentThread is unavailable in this Unity Mono runtime: known allocation probe did not advance it. Earlier microbench zero-byte fields are invalid, not evidence of zero allocations; later rows mark unavailable and use -1. Only raw-profiler GC bytes are used for allocation comparison.",
    "Crowd positions are staged but engine random behavior, contact order and actual entity/projectile counts can vary. The captures compare the same stress policy, not identical per-tick world states.",
    "The stat-crowd-geometry timing sample overlapped a Unity build and is excluded from timing comparisons; its timing-limit.json preserves that qualification.",
    "The full normal R21 run and its measured wall-time excess remain separate evidence. These captures identify allocation costs and effects of bounded fixes, but do not by themselves quantify the resulting normal-run wall-time change."
  ],
